# Merge lane for every repository this machine hosts (sd:3003). One job file,
# the same on every machine: `lane run --hosted` runs the lane of each managed
# repository whose lane host is this machine, side by side. `NULL` means
# the hub. Move a repository's lane with `sd-db repo lane-host <path>
# <host>|hub` or the dashboard's Move lane control; the next run follows it.
# It replaces one job file per repository, hub or satellite.
#
# It needs no `-C`: it reads the repo table, not a working folder. A lane
# whose runner lock is held is skipped and never waited for. The job drains
# each queue and exits; it is not a poller, and an empty queue exits 0 at once.
#
# The run starts no lane at its 40-minute budget, hands off each lane
# still running and exits (pack sd:9332). launchd runs one instance of a
# job at a time, so the next slot starts a fresh run; it skips the lanes
# a handed-off child holds. Each handed-off child TERMs itself at the
# run's TERM point.
#
# CRON_JOBS_TIMEOUT_GRACE is 30 s, not the wrapper's 10 s, so a lane's
# TERM unwind (about 5 s per ship group) ends before the wrapper's KILL,
# with room for a gate that ignores TERM; a KILL before it ends leaves
# sd-ship sessions with no record (pack sd:9392).
#
# JOB_TIMEOUT is above one lane run on purpose (review, `make check` and a
# merge take 30-60 minutes): a run still waits for a lane it cannot hand
# off, and a limit below that could stop a merge part way.
#
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/5 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="120m"
CRON_JOBS_TIMEOUT_GRACE=30
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/bin/sd-ship\" lane run --hosted"
